 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Thermal mounting",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Maximum RθJA is 55 °C/W with the part on 1 in² of 2 oz copper and rises to 175 °C/W on a minimum pad of 2 oz copper. RθJC is fixed by the device; RθJA depends on the board."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Board attachment",
   "page": 15,
   "text": "The underside pad goes onto a matching copper land. Thermal vias of 0.2 mm diameter in the centre pad are optional; the suggested rows sit 0.975 mm apart, with 0.905 mm between the vias of the outer rows. The land pattern is solder-mask defined, with at least 0.05 mm of mask clearance on every side. A 0.125 mm stencil with four openings on the centre pad gives 76 % paste coverage of it; paste may release better from laser-cut openings that have rounded corners and trapezoidal walls."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Handling",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "ESD protection on the part is limited; keep the leads shorted or the part in conductive foam while stored or handled so the gate oxide is not damaged. Moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 at a 260 °C peak, compatible with lead-free IR and convection reflow."
  }
 ],
